 "text": "9/29/26, 9:39 AM\nWhen you create a move-in, the system proposes an existing meter reading result for all the billing-relevant registers allocated to\nthe devices for billing purposes. Ensure you have configured the system accordingly in Customizing under |*SAP Utilities\nDevice Management Meter Reading \u00bb Basic Settings Define Control Parameters for Meter Reading Data Processing\n\ne Ifthe system proposes a meter reading result then choose one of the following two options:\n\ne If you adopt the meter reading result, the system adds the meter reading reason Move-in to the result.\n\ne If you change the meter reading result, a new result is created with the meter reading reason Move-in.\n\ne Ifthe system does not propose a meter reading result, you can have it estimate a result or enter one manually. In both\ncases, the system creates a new meter reading result from the adopted/changed result and gives it the meter reading\nreason Move-In.\n\ne Ifthe system does not propose a meter reading result, and you do not enter one manually, a service notification or service\norder is created for the current register. For more information see service notifications and orders .\n\nYou can also suppress the meter reading proposal or define an interval as required. If you do this, the system only makes a\nproposal if the meter reading result on which the proposal is based was takes during the interval. Ensure you have configured the\n\nsystem accordingly in Customizing under |)*SAP Utilities \u00bb Device Management \u00bb Meter Reading \u00bb Basic Settings \u00bb Define\nControl Parameters for Meter Reading Data Processing 5 . Ensure that you make an appropriate entry in the Move-in prop. inter.\n(Interval for determining default value) and the Display default move-in value checkbox alongside it.\n\nYou can find additional information on meter reading data processing in the section on the meter reading component.\n\nBudget Billing Plan\n\nUse\n\nYou can create a budget billing plan for every contract involved in a move-in, provided the BB procedure (budget billing plan active)\n\nfield in the contract account contains the value 1 (Statistical procedure for budget billing collection) or 2 (Debit entry procedure for\nbudget billing collection). You have the following options:\n\ne Create budget billing plan manually\nTo do this, choose the Budget billing plan pushbutton in move-in processing.\n\ne Create budget billing plan when data is saved\n\nTo have the system create a budget billing plan automatically when you save the move-in document, make the appropriate entry in\nthe Create budget billing plan field in Customizing under |}'Move-In/Out \u00bb Move-In \u00bb Define Move-In Control Parameters on\nContract Level.\n\nIf necessary, you can also override the settings you have established in Customizing. To do this, choose |sExtras Control\nParameters Jin move-in processing.\n\nYou can choose whether to assign a budget billing amount that is valid for all due dates, or whether to have each amount\ncalculated by the system.\n\nThe budget billing due dates are result from the Scheduling component. The printout date of the first budget billing due date\n\nae 8 ge\n",
